eye-contact-co-processing-at-the-speed-of-light-lines-10 : List (List Word)
eye-contact-co-processing-at-the-speed-of-light-lines-10 = cons "## 7. Coupled Co-Processors and Evolved Optical Machinery" (cons "" (cons "Bidirectional gaze couples two dynamical systems $(x_A, x_B)$ with intrinsic relaxation rates $\eta_A, \eta_B > 0$ and optical coupling gains $\gamma_{AB}, \gamma_{BA}$: $\dot{x}_A = -\eta_A x_A + \gamma_{AB} x_B$ and $\dot{x}_B = \gamma_{BA} x_A - \eta_B x_B$. As established in `neuro/eye-contact.hypercubical` (`ec-bidirectional-lyapunov-sos-id`), a weighted Lyapunov energy $V = p_A x_A^2 + p_B x_B^2$ certifies an exact stability boundary:" (cons "" (cons "$$4 p_A p_B \eta_A \eta_B > (p_A \gamma_{AB} + p_B \gamma_{BA})^2$$" (cons "" (cons "Below this threshold, mutual gaze settles into bounded co-regulatory equilibrium (joint attention, affective synchrony, cooperative alignment). Crossing it drives runaway positive feedback—mutual pupillary contagion, dominance escalation, or acute tension resolved only by breaking gaze. Two people in eye contact form a temporary coupled co-processor that reaches states neither nervous system would reach alone." (cons "" (cons "Human anatomy reflects sustained selection pressure for this coupling: uniquely conspicuous white sclera among primates (the cooperative eye hypothesis), fine-grained periocular musculature, and dedicated neural circuitry across the fusiform face area (FFA), posterior superior temporal sulcus (pSTS), and amygdala." (cons "" nil)))))))))
